using $2\leq C_*$, and \eqref{eq:induction hypothesis for realzzz} follows directly from the definition \eqref{eq:alphak recurrence rel} of $\alpha_k$. 

\smallskip 

\noindent 2. \textit{Uniform boundedness}. We have $ \Vert A_k \Vert_{L^\infty([0,t])}^{1/n_k} \leq C_*^{\alpha_{k}/n_k}(M_1+M_2)$ and thus it suffices to show that $\alpha_k/n_k$ is bounded. Dividing \eqref{eq:alphak recurrence rel} by $n_k=2^k$ and rewriting $n_k=2n_{k-1}$, 
